
Usage: /TAP <username>
  A  SysOp  command  to  wire tap the user, so that whatever a user is
  whispering,  you'll  "hear" it.  The user who is whispering does not
  know  you  are doing this.  This command should only be used to keep
  the integrity of the system, and should not be used for pleasure.

  Example:
     /TAP crook

  See Also:
     /UNTAP

